  "question": {
    "text": "Suppose that all the terms of an arithmetic progression (A.P.) are natural numbers. If the ratio of the sum of the first seven terms to the sum of the first eleven terms is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>11</mn></math> and the seventh terms lies in between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>130</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>140</mn></math>, then the common difference of this A.P. is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>[</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>[</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> <br > <math><mo>⇒</mo><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> <br > <math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>d</mi></math> <br >Also   <math><mn>130</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>140</mn></math> <br > <math><mn>130</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>15</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>140</mn></math> <br > <math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>",
